`insert_only` mode is especially useful when [migrating from one embedding model to another](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-operations/embedding-model-migration/), where conflicts between regular updates and background re-embedding tasks need to be resolved.

<img alt="Embedding model migration in blue-green deployment" src="https://qdrant.tech/docs/embedding-model-migration.png" width="80%">

Embedding model migration in blue-green deployment

`update_only` mode is useful with [conditional updates](#conditional-updates). Because upserts default to inserts for non-existing points, a conditional update without an explicit `update_mode` will insert a new point even if the condition is not met, which is not the intended behavior in most cases.

