[](#hybrid-search-using-qdrant-cloud-inference)Hybrid Search Using Qdrant Cloud Inference
==========

|Time: 30 min|Level: Intermediate|
|------------|-------------------|

In this tutorial, we’ll walkthrough building a **hybrid semantic search engine** using Qdrant Cloud’s built-in [inference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/inference/) capabilities. You’ll learn how to:

* Automatically embed your data using [cloud Inference](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/cloud/inference/) without needing to run local models,
* Combine dense semantic embeddings with [sparse BM25 keywords](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-basics/reranking-hybrid-search/), and
* Perform hybrid search using [Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)](https://qdrant.tech/documentation/search/hybrid-queries/) to retrieve the most relevant results.

